  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 246 AM EDT Wed Jun 10 2026\n\nLong term starts Thu night into Fri morning where moisture remains \nin place across the southeast. Forecast PWATs are not expected to be \nas high as they have been but still expecting values in the 0.5\" to \n1\" range. The Bermuda ridge axis will have slide a bit further south \n(across central FL) as we get into the end of the week. This will \nallow a frontal boundary that begins to develop across the Northern \nplains Thu, to move SE across the MS and OH river valleys Fri and \ninto NW GA late Fri night. This front appears to make its way south \nand stall some where across central or south GA Sat then washing out \nand getting caught in the W to SWLY flow around the top side of the \nold Bermuda ridge. This front lingers through the weekend keeping \nmoisture around and diurnal chances of showers and storms in place. \nWe'll also see temperatures climb into the 90s in many areas Friday \nand Saturday ahead of the main system, which will bring heat indices \ninto the mid to upper 90s for the first time in a while. \n\nBoth the GFS and ECMWF continue to show a weak tropical system \ndeveloping across the southern Gulf Thu/Fri and pushing into the \neast coast of Mexico around daybreak Sat. As it pushes onshore it \nmoves Northward around the periphery of the old ridge and gets \ncaught in the westerly flow making its way east across LA/MS Sun \ninto Mon. If this pattern continues we could be dealing with some \ndeep moisture across GA by Tue/Wed of next week. Will continue to \nkeep an eye on how this develops.",
